{"direct":{"NURSERY":"msg.ef7e199166ce5d59","WATER":"msg.556728f7f45600ac","GARDEN":"msg.4d9ca3ee5a334632","LETTER":"msg.f03df439a7c9cf27","WE BEGIN AGAIN":"msg.89157a3a85f6b28a","ROOM FOR TOMORROW":"msg.f550bad1ce42a867","A CITY OF NAMES":"msg.e579757a942205b8","The nursery key":"msg.271c777d7c1c8f8f","A packet of seeds":"msg.4f1274e4532ae95d","Mara, the caretaker":"msg.a3d3a6a5f6e91c65","THE DOOR CAN OPEN AGAIN":"msg.1ff93791ead7d38f","The headline has changed. The hinges have not. We will still have to open the door ourselves.":"msg.36c679248020311c","The nursery key is on the old roof, beyond three paper ledges. Bring it back and I will let the morning in.":"msg.a8aa1fd8bf0751e8","I have kept the cradles clean. There is a difference between waiting for the world to end and making room for it to continue.":"msg.daff46bea6135179","Ivo, the apprentice":"msg.892559e272a77095","A FORECAST THAT CAN BE REPAIRED":"msg.75dfb602beb8af01","I used to draw the future as a machine. This one actually needs repairing.":"msg.437629bf8a78069c","Open the waterwheel housing. When the marked vane turns green, give it a cry. Three aligned notes will bring the water back.":"msg.156b04c3be8c219d","Once it flows, the greenhouse can share its seeds. A prediction cannot grow anything. Water can.":"msg.747a2e0baf1cf7bd","Ada, the typesetter":"msg.62fdca99530ca58a","THE FIRST LETTER OF THE NEW EDITION":"msg.2cc2f8ab094a5986","For once, the page is blank because we have not lived it yet.":"msg.6fc1d293938fe246","Open the nursery, restore the water, and plant the garden. Then meet me at the small press to choose the first words we send out.":"msg.cf524725a1e5069e","The postbox is on the high roof to the east. The new drafts will carry a letter as easily as they carry a pair of impossible ears.":"msg.0062beaff425a208","E  VISIT THE OPEN NURSERY":"msg.74d248a8f307913a","E  OPEN THE NURSERY":"msg.2355c346ade9e927","E  ASK ABOUT THE KEY":"msg.b3b4680f72344a72","E  LISTEN TO THE WATER":"msg.9ff0690e2af320e8","CRY WHEN THE VANE IS GREEN":"msg.347b69856723ae98","E  OPEN THE WATERWHEEL":"msg.aeea9d0bc544be11","E  WATCH THE GARDEN":"msg.3eec469a93d3eb22","E  PLANT A PACKET OF SEEDS":"msg.badf5ac797d7c363","FIND SEEDS IN THE WATERED GREENHOUSE":"msg.79b1b4686a7616b5","E  READ THE NEW HEADLINE":"msg.cda71a45e3995669","E  REVISE THE LETTER":"msg.ffbe469a4d9a20bd","E  WRITE THE FIRST LETTER":"msg.6e3cf58d9cf77397","E  PLAN THE FIRST LETTER":"msg.5fe13d872a59f7b1","E  READ THE FIRST EDITION":"msg.ee7a261ad4f7b333","E  POST THE FIRST LETTER":"msg.3bdb5d2cd47f7c9d","A LETTER IS STILL WAITING TO BE WRITTEN":"msg.1afcd6b25341c4cc","E  LISTEN TO {v0}":"msg.7de030f2223365d1","E  LISTEN TO ":"msg.4a31043b52cd9ebb","THE CITY IS OPEN. THERE IS ROOM TO STAY.":"msg.4f3ff225a75389f1","BRING THE KEY BACK TO MARA’S NURSERY ←":"msg.bbf22e46e2d8934b","FIND THE NURSERY KEY ON THE OLD ROOF →":"msg.359869adb0a18b30","OPEN IVO’S WATERWHEEL HOUSING →":"msg.5be3d8a6bb03c15c","VANE ALIGNED — CRY AT THE WATERWHEEL":"msg.69969d48b7ad8efa","WAIT FOR THE GREEN VANE  /  {v0} OF 3 NOTES":"msg.c4a62a5913955723","WAIT FOR THE GREEN VANE  /  ":"msg.992f701f1ff64242"," OF 3 NOTES":"msg.1ce22d9d29068768","GATHER THE GREENHOUSE SEEDS. PLANT THE THREE BEDS.":"msg.f8b39d1e218fb6b3","MEET ADA AT THE SMALL PRESS. CHOOSE THE FIRST WORDS →":"msg.e5cd5113198338ed","CARRY THE FIRST LETTER TO THE ROOFTOP POSTBOX →":"msg.adf82b014310474b","Body":"msg.6ccaa6415b5ee449","Display":"msg.34e108c0896d0158","Mono":"msg.6f00156cec078cc0","KEEPER OF THE EMPTY NURSERY":"msg.2516e68af36a90b3","They boarded up the nursery after reading the headline. I kept the keys. A prediction does not get to lock a door.":"msg.78427b29e2dcc362","I folded the children’s unfinished stories into paper cranes. There are three in this district. Bring them back into the light.":"msg.c0b4cae985c45e27","The proofreader beside the chimney can change STILL to RISING. Open the draft, spread your ears, and follow the paper.":"msg.3c7d3f4ac748b242","There are two chimes above the old ink channel. Carry one note to the other before it fades. I kept some silk for your ears; the marginalia can show you what it would change.":"msg.53e448aadf1bb4a4","STILL":"msg.14472991965de4c8","RISING":"msg.98dba6ddfac80c0b","A rising draft opens a path above the ink.":"msg.3228b82d6224f386","The Unfinished Lullaby":"msg.969219c1f2d1564b","Mara never wrote a final verse. A lullaby is a promise to meet again in the morning.":"msg.fe2041b5e934ecbd","A Pair of Small Shoes":"msg.f2a5cf50b6a0fcfa","Someone left room inside them for feet that had not yet grown. Hope sometimes looks like an ordinary purchase.":"msg.54d60a8c04e8a19d","The Nursery Key":"msg.01cbad5e425a3708","The city sealed the door. Its caretaker kept making copies of the key.":"msg.b80314720fa70344","ASSISTANT TO THE CHIEF FORECASTER":"msg.c283a84bc971df10","They asked me to draw the future as a straight line. Every time I drew a branch, they sent it back.":"msg.b2a91b7e058894f4","The factory’s proofreader changes FIXED to MOVING. The delivery lift still remembers how to travel.":"msg.237ff15646cbfaf6","Listen to the presses. Red means prepare, the stamp means move, and the quiet afterward belongs to you.":"msg.b9c1efc7e488b994","The redactors print NO at anyone who passes. A well-timed cry can return it as IF. One of the margin chimes rides the delivery lift. Its partner is waiting on the roof.":"msg.1e0561356ac77d41","FIXED":"msg.f28b69013846df29","MOVING":"msg.d40436f6037a8ac5","The delivery lift now travels across the ink.":"msg.b9db1b11cb4c7761","A Forecast with Branches":"msg.6d9c3519f0938369","Ivo’s rejected diagram contains seven different tomorrows. None of them is a dead end.":"msg.69a848e99986f114","The Blank Column":"msg.e44fa3dfeb72710c","One worker left a column empty rather than invent a number. It was the most honest thing the factory printed.":"msg.4811b66519a10ad9","A Letter Never Posted":"msg.71f5b81302255823","“I cannot promise what the world will be like. I can promise there will be someone waiting for you.”":"msg.dd7ddf2d891e3b96","LAST EMPLOYEE OF TOMORROW’S PRESS":"msg.ad1dc5fdd6b7560d","A headline has very little room for a person. That never stopped the editors from trying to fit everyone into one.":"msg.64ac7e2064a93f59","Change CERTAIN to POSSIBLE. Bridges that the newspaper forgot will become solid beneath your feet.":"msg.624c4ad740525040","At the final press, wait for the stamp to fall. During its quiet interval, cry beside each of the three proof plates. Then print your correction.":"msg.77019efcedae39e2","Two more chimes wait before the final ink channel. A possible world can carry their echo. If every margin opens, the next edition can leave room for more than a single future.":"msg.48972e4b25de984f","CERTAIN":"msg.bdd28f488fe30ae8","POSSIBLE":"msg.49ed77f8cd66eb4c","The possible bridges are now solid paper.":"msg.6322367fd7001fcb","The Typesetter’s Name":"msg.ea9e25aa5e9c3ae8","Ada set other people’s words for forty years. This is the first page on which she put her own name.":"msg.3f0cfec3e73d2da8","A Drawing of Wings":"msg.fabf899e82b63fda","The newspaper called the ears a defect. In the margin, someone drew air beneath them.":"msg.a9eedfdfb8365907","Tomorrow, Unnumbered":"msg.dae2eeb8b5547ef4","A date was never written on this page. There was no need to decide how far the story could go.":"msg.31e551817ea145b4","THE FIRST MORNING":"msg.2efc82c89ecf61e4","DRY":"msg.5eca1a91a6b4f1d7","FLOWING":"msg.36c49a3483bbf704","The greenhouse and the high drafts have water again.":"msg.32b01ac04a57f30b","CRY":"msg.c9180d0339e7858e","JUMP":"msg.f8b3c726c4df49d1","USE":"msg.b3c2ed23b44e753d","Cry beside the wheel when the marked vane is green. Three aligned notes restore the water.":"msg.5688f31a7814626c","Something has begun to grow here.":"msg.3b2f5952d818b288","Gather seed packets from the greenhouse ledges after restoring the water.":"msg.ddcf2c4b885f983c","Ada is waiting at the small press. The first 